# Accessibility & UI Standards (Shield / WCAG 2.2 AAA)

### 1. Contrast & Targets
- Contrast: 7:1 for normal text, 3:1 for UI controls and graphical objects.
- Min text size: 14px (0.875rem).
- Touch target sizes: Minimum 44×44px (48×48px recommended).

### 2. Button as Link — Use `buttonVariants`, NEVER `<Button asChild>`

Our Base UI Button applies `role="button"`, which strips native link semantics.

```tsx
// ❌ WRONG
<Button asChild variant="outline">
  <Link href="/admin/cv">Open CV editor</Link>
</Button>

// ✅ CORRECT
import { buttonVariants } from "@/components/ui/button";
import { Link } from "@/i18n/routing";

<Link
  href="/admin/cv"
  className={buttonVariants({ variant: "outline", size: "sm" })}
>
  Open CV editor
</Link>
```

### 3. Iconography & Emojis — No Raw Unicode Emojis in Copy or Translations

```tsx
// ❌ WRONG — raw emojis in copy or translation files
"scheduleCall": "📅 Schedule a video call"
<button>⚡ Quick action</button>

// ✅ CORRECT — Lucide / React Icons in JSX
import { Calendar, Zap } from "lucide-react";

<div className="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5">
  <Zap className="size-3.5 text-primary" />
  <span>{t("quickAction")}</span>
</div>
```

### 4. Animations — Use `motion/react`, NEVER `framer-motion`

```tsx
// ❌ WRONG
import { motion } from "framer-motion";

// ✅ CORRECT
import { motion } from "motion/react";
```
